add('Grammar questions','Nderuin disagrees with the app’s plural-ending entries',['Nderu','-n','-in'],'The example has nderuin. The app’s -n entry says vowel-ending nouns take -n, while -in is for consonant-ending nouns. Nderu ends in a vowel. Both pieces of app content cannot be followed as one exception-free rule.','Keep the attested example until you decide: document an exception, adjust the rule, or approve nderun.',[2059],certainty='Direct mismatch')
add('Grammar questions','The same citizen sentence is both singular and plural',['Welrin'],'Exactly the same Celan sentence is translated once as “The citizens vote” and once as “The citizen votes.” Other examples also leave number unmarked. This may be permitted, but the learner needs to know when plural endings are optional.','Clarify whether number is inferred from context here; otherwise choose matching number marking.',[1298,1321])
add('Grammar questions','Some nouns act as verbs without a displayed verb sense',['Shen','Kal','Bren','Vanesh','Jor','Kar','Shara','Xar','Shentalzhael'],'These words have examples meaning measure/count, strengthen, harvest, trade, surge, strike, follow, shelter, or triage, but their entries do not consistently show those action readings. That may be valid Celan word conversion; it is not explained by the entry labels alone.','Decide whether a shared noun-to-verb rule covers them or individual action senses should be shown.',[834,851,866,1407,1566,1626,1643,1645,1655,1679,1682,1973])
